live-busybox
============

Static busybox for the MX/antiX live-initrd (mx-iso-template).
Source: Debian busybox (debian/patches is Debian's patch set, unchanged).

Only one flavour is built: "live", configured by debian/config/pkg/live.
It is linked statically against musl (musl-gcc from musl-tools). Kernel
headers are made visible to musl-gcc via symlinks in b/kernel-headers.

musl differences vs. the old uClibc/glibc builds:
  - FEATURE_VI_REGEX_SEARCH is off (needs GNU regex API), plain vi search works
  - no ERE back-references inside the pattern (grep -E '(ab)\1')
  - \< followed by an empty-matching expression (awk gsub(/\<b*/,...))
  - date -d does not accept a timezone inside the date string
  The two affected testsuite cases are removed by debian/testsuite-musl.diff.

debian/config/reference/ holds, for comparison only (not used in the build):
  mx-busybox-1.31.1.config   config recovered from the old initrd busybox
                             ("busybox bbconfig"), the origin of pkg/live
  deb static udeb            Debian's flavour configs of this version

Changing the configuration / new upstream version
-------------------------------------------------
The build fails if the shipped config differs from what oldconfig
generates (e.g. new upstream options). To update:

  mkdir /tmp/bbcfg && cp debian/config/pkg/live /tmp/bbcfg/.config
  make -C /tmp/bbcfg -f $PWD/Makefile KBUILD_SRC=$PWD oldconfig   # or menuconfig
  cp /tmp/bbcfg/.config debian/config/pkg/live

Keep the applet set in sync with what the live-initrd uses; new applets
default to "y" in oldconfig - say "n" unless needed.

Building both architectures
---------------------------
  amd64:  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
  i386:   build in an i386 chroot, e.g. sbuild --arch=i386 / pbuilder
